  "chapter": 712,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 52 Chapter 712\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 7081, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the agriculture and markets law, in relation to\n        establishing the agrivoltaics research program\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require the Cornell College of  Agriculture  and  Life\nSciences  (CALS)  to  establish  an  agrivoltaics  research  program and\nconduct, support, and develop technologies  and  management  strategies,\nalong  with  verifications  systems  to  facilitate  the sustainable and\nresilient co-location of crops and photovoltaics.\n \n  I support the goals of this legislation, which would  expand  research\ninto  this  evolving area of study and could provide unique solutions to\nthe land use issues related to solar siting on agricultural land. Howev-\ner, technical changes were necessary to reference the existing appropri-\nation for this work.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact these chang-\nes.  On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2023
 },
